Target shape (19 insns): n=root; if(!n) return NULL; e=n->first; GUARD beql e,0 -> outer test (delay: n=n->next); val=e->key; INNER bnel val,key,-> bottom test (delay: e=e->next); jr; move v0,v1 (== return e); bottom test: bnel e,0,-> the val-load block (delay: val=e->key); n=n->next; outer bnel n,0,-> the guard (delay: e=n->first); jr; move v0,zero (return NULL). So: the inner loop is BOTTOM-tested (rotated: the e->key reload sits in the back-edge delay slot) and the key comparison branches OVER the inline `return e` epilogue.
